sections.thingsIMayWantToChange:
I may ask you to change:
- **the tree**: add, remove, rename, re-describe or re-order nodes, and change the dependencies;
- **the settings**: title, language, what the learners are called, the everyday word for the subject, what students get sloppy about in writing;
- **the teaching instructions.** The defaults are published at aiskilltrees.com/prompts/, each section under a keyword that is also printed in front of it in the instruction students get (`tone: …`). To change a section, add a `prompt` row holding only that section; the rest stays default. "No emoji" or "stricter about showing working" is a `prompt` row, not an edit to every node. Look up section names rather than inventing them; an unknown name is reported as an error.
